UPDATE public.blog_articles SET direct_answer='Evidence for knee joint supplements is strongest for glucosamine sulphate, UC-II collagen, chondroitin sulphate, Boswellia serrata, bioavailable curcumin and high-dose omega-3, with oral hyaluronic acid as a possible addition. It stresses product quality, pharmaceutical-grade forms and third-party testing, and says supplements should sit alongside weight management, physiotherapy, medical care and GP advice.' WHERE slug='best-supplement-for-knee-joint';
UPDATE public.blog_articles SET direct_answer='For arthritis, the guide advises limiting ultra-processed foods, sugary drinks, refined carbohydrates, omega-6-rich vegetable oils and fried foods, alcohol, especially beer for gout, high-salt processed foods and sometimes full-fat dairy. It says these can worsen inflammation, uric acid, swelling and joint pain, while wholegrains, oily fish, vegetables, olive oil, nuts and seeds are suggested swaps.' WHERE slug='foods-to-avoid-with-arthritis';
UPDATE public.blog_articles SET direct_answer='The article says telling your employer about arthritis can help if done early and met with understanding, because supportive disclosure may improve job retention, reduce symptom interference and enable reasonable adjustments. It advises discussing concerns with your GP or rheumatologist, tracking symptoms, preparing clear work-related requests, knowing your rights, and seeking help if symptoms worsen.' WHERE slug='should-you-tell-your-employer-about-your-arthritis';
UPDATE public.blog_articles SET direct_answer='Progress with arthritis can be tracked simply by checking three weekly markers: pain on waking, the longest pain-free interval and one functional win. The guide recommends small, consistent steps: graded movement, anti-inflammatory eating, weight management, heat or cold and better sleep. Seek GP or physiotherapist advice for hot swollen joints, weight loss, prolonged morning stiffness, numbness or weakness.' WHERE slug='expert-qa-track-progress-without-measuring';